  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**: The optimization landscape is high-dimensional and non-convex. We address this with an adaptive resolution method. Start at a coarse grid and dynamically increase resolution when local minima are suspected. This uses a hierarchical optimization scheme: first constraint optimization, then greedy local search, and finally refinement at increased resolution. Progress is monitored by the rate of improvement and the local gradient behavior.\n\n  2. **Mathematical Specification**: \n    - Let \\( h(x) \\) be defined on grid \\( \\mathbb{Z}_{n} \\), periodic in \\( [0, 2] \\).\n    - Objective: Minimize \\( C_5 = \\max_{k} dx \\times \\text{np.max}(\\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, \\text{mode}='full')) \\).\n    - Constraints: \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1, \\sum h_i = n/2 \\).\n    - Representation: Store \\( h \\) as a real array of length \\( n \\).\n    - Objective Function: \\( C_5 = dx \\times \\max_{\\text{lags}} \\| \\text{corr}_{ii} \\| \\)\n    - Solve projection: \\( \\min_{\\|\\phi\\|^2} \\text{subject to} \\| \\nabla_{\\phi} \\mathcal{L} \\|_2 \\leq \\epsilon \\) where \\( \\mathcal{L} = \\text{C5} \\).\n\n  3. **Implementation Procedure**:\n    - Phase 1: Coarse Solution Initialization\n      - Set \\( n_0 = 60 \\), \\( \\alpha = 1.5 \\), \\( \\epsilon = 0.0005 \\)\n      - Use projected gradient with box constraints and projection step.\n      - \\( h^{(0)} = \\text{smooth\\_get}(n_0, \\alpha) \\)\n      - For \\( k = 1 \\) iterations until timeout or stalling:\n        - Project \\( h \\) to satisfy constraints: \\( h \\leftarrow \\text{project\\_to\\_sum}(h, n_0/2) \\)\n        - Compute gradient: \\( \\nabla h = \\text{gradient\\_estimate}(h) \\)\n        - Gradient clipping: \\( \\| \\nabla h \\|_{\\infty} \\leq \\epsilon \\)\n        - Symmetric step: \\( h \\leftarrow h + \\text{symmetric\\_step}(\\nabla h) \\)\n        - If no improvement or stalling, double resolution: \\( n_{k+1} = 2 \\times n_k \\)\n\n    - Phase 2: Local Search Refinement\n      - Use coordinate descent with adaptive step length\n      - Step lengths: geometric progression \\( \\{ 0.01, 0.005, 0.001 \\} \\)\n      - Maintain two best candidates: global and local relative to current solution\n      - Use countersteepest ascent until improvement threshold \\( \\delta = 5 \\times 10^{-5} \\)\n\n    - Phase 3: Resolution Upgrade\n      - Trigger condition: Gradient norm \\( \\|\\nabla h\\| > 5 \\times 10^{-4} \\)\n      - New resolution: double grid points \\( n_{\\text{new}} = 2n \\)\n      - Reinitialize projection: \\( h_{\\text{new}} = \\text{linear\\_interp}(h_{\\text{old}}, n_{\\text{old}}, n_{\\text{new}}) \\)\n      - Repeat constraints and projections\n\n  4. **Search Choices**: \n    - Pivotal choice: Resolution doubling when gradient violates \\( 5 \\times 10^{-4} \\) vs. C5 improvement stops.\n    - Algorithm variation: Sums of squares gradient replacement for symmetric positions.\n    - Tolerance: Gradient-based steps only if relative improvement > \\( 2 \\times 10^{-3} \\)\n\n  5. **Budget and Robustness**:\n    - BaseGrid (60 points): 100 seconds\n    - CoarseGrid (120 pts): 200 seconds\n    - BaseGrid: 360 pts -> 600 seconds\n    - Timeout detection: Progress stalling if improvement per 10 iterations < 1e-6\n    - Early exit if grid size exceeds memory limits for n=1280 points (max)\n    - Fall back to CoarseGrid solution if timeout\n\n  6. **Validation and Output**: \n    - Final phase: LocalSearch refinement\n    - Final output: \\( (h, \\text{compute\\_c5}(h), \\text{len}(h)) \\)\n    - Validation checks: Feasibility (\\( \\sum h_i \\ll n/2 \\)), non-negativity, normalization.\n    - Dimension transfer: Interpolation and projection maintained during resolution change.\n    - Safety: Gradient normalization bounds, integer step iterations, no floating-point rounding until output.",
